window.DIGEST.foryou.push(...[{"id": "2112578026357825830", "url": "https://x.com/via_ai_/status/2112578026357825830", "text": "Today we’re coming out of stealth to give enterprises frontier AI coding at half the cost.\n\nVia is a middleware that sits between a CLI / IDE and an LLM, installs in 10 seconds, and has already demonstrated a new standard of performance.\n\n- On DeepSWE 1.1, Claude Code (Opus 5.5) is 306% the cost of Via US (US-model-only configuration). Via US is equally accurate.\n\n- On Terminal Bench 4.0, Claude Code (Opus 5.5) is 150% the cost of Via. Via is more accurate.\n\nVia runs inside your VPC, so no data leaves your environment.\n\nWe’re in production at a public healthcare company, with trials underway at several of the largest tech companies in Silicon Valley. We have room for five more enterprises before the end of the year: pilot@via.dev\n\nOur co-founder @ilaamathur on why we built Via:", "name": "Via", "handle": "via_ai_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1953218687152078848/dkBaVdYI_200x200.jpg", "likes": 19, "rts": 5, "replies": 8, "views": 1034, "ts": 1792512825, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112575743792415005", "url": "https://x.com/ilaamathur/status/2112575743792415005", "text": "Today, @via_ai_ is coming out of stealth to provide enterprises frontier AI coding at half the cost.\n\nWe are a team of Olympiad camp qualifiers (with multiple gold medals), researchers, and repeat founders from Stanford and IIT.\n\nVia is backed by @jeffawilke (ex-CEO Amazon Worldwide Consumer), @manikgupta (ex-Uber CPO), @shaileshrao (ex-Google MD), and other legends from Anthropic, Apple, Snowflake, and Twitter.\n\n@ShrayAlag and I left Stanford CS to build Codegraph, an LLM-optimized compression algorithm. Codegraph put Via at the top of SWE-Bench Verified for several months of 2025, ahead of Anthropic, OpenAI, Cognition, and Cursor (single model, no test-time compute).\n\nNow, we’re bringing this research, alongside our new Umami agent architecture, to market. Via integrates in 10 seconds with any CLI / IDE and runs within your enterprise’s VPC.\n\nOn benchmarks, Via and Via US (US-only models) set a new standard of performance:\n\n- On DeepSWE v1.1, Claude Code (Opus 5.5) is 306% the cost of Via US. Via US is equally accurate.\n      • Devin Fusion is 244% the cost of Via US, Cursor Router is 294%.\n\n- On Terminal Bench 4.0, Claude Code (Opus 5.5) is 150% the cost of Via. Via is more accurate.\n     • Devin Fusion is 155% the cost of Via, Cursor Router is 134%.\n\nWe are in production at a public healthcare company, with trials underway at several of the largest tech companies in Silicon Valley.\n\nWe have room for 5 more enterprises before the end of the year. DM me or email pilot@via.dev and we’ll get back to you very soon.\n\nSee the comments for how Via would deploy for your team.", "name": "Ila Mathur", "handle": "ilaamathur", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2014807779832430593/woZBXetJ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 208, "rts": 26, "replies": 56, "views": 28682, "ts": 1792512281, "media": [{"type": "gif", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/tweet_video/HVFgPc4aMAAQpLS.mp4", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/tweet_video/HVFgPc4aMAAQpLS.mp4", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/tweet_video_thumb/HVFgPc4aMAAQpLS.jpg", "dur": 0}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.1, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112522747255341157", "url": "https://x.com/lumixsv/status/2112522747255341157", "text": "It is becoming f*cking dangerous\n\ni set 300 Grok @bot workers loose on 100 companies overnight. one cheap checker bot watched all of them, and i went to sleep\n\ni opened the dashboard at 7am:\n- 300 bots in 5 teams. sites, prices, reviews, hiring, owners\n- every claim checked against its page in ~100 ms\n- pass 1 caught 47 made-up facts. pass 2 caught 12. pass 3 caught zero\n- all 100 profiles landed in my Obsidian notes\n\neveryone's scared of AI making stuff up. most people still ask the same AI to check itself\n\nthe rule i'd steal first: the bots that find things never grade their own work. a cheaper bot asks one question, \"where did you see this?\"\n\nevery red flash on the right is a bot getting caught, kinda hypnotic. by 0:20 there are none left\n\nhonestly the checker matters more than the 300. without it you get 300 confident guesses\n\nan analyst needs weeks for 100 profiles. i slept through mine\n\ntry it today with no bots. paste any AI answer into a fresh chat and ask for the link behind every number\n\nbookmark this. the checker prompt is in the first reply, the full Grok Bot setup is in the article below\n\nwhat's the first job you'd hand 300 bots?", "name": "Lumix", "handle": "lumixsv", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2088512605883158528/8mYeFA--_200x200.jpg", "likes": 25, "rts": 6, "replies": 8, "views": 1060, "ts": 1792499646, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112522649188364288/vid/avc1/720x900/gS8qta95m5cqqE18.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112522649188364288/vid/avc1/1080x1350/_CKgaH58CJ7RVWJE.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112522649188364288/img/FDsJYxSAiR-vzzq3.jpg", "dur": 23}], "quote": {"id": "2110007684976030097", "url": "https://x.com/savipww/status/2110007684976030097", "text": "https://x.com/i/article/2109953490990534656", "name": "savip.", "handle": "savipww", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2051547758679457793/VLPGnK4K_200x200.jpg", "likes": 295, "rts": 38, "replies": 31, "views": 486713, "ts": 1791900008, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.1, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112582138105405725", "url": "https://x.com/So8res/status/2112582138105405725", "text": "Tbc I think it'd be great to have additional watchdogs that had an ability to see through the company bullshit and that *didn't* have any sort of social ties. It might even be better. But the voluntary nature of the relationship is an enormous source of distortion either way.", "name": "Nate Soares ⏹️", "handle": "So8res", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1935185891863273472/2RB6s6TS_200x200.jpg", "likes": 42, "rts": 0, "replies": 3, "views": 985, "ts": 1792513806, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": "2112581339216273813", "cat": "Research & Safety", "score": 5.09, "thread": [{"id": "2112581339216273813", "url": "https://x.com/So8res/status/2112581339216273813", "text": "You worry that METR is not independent enough because its employees have some social connections to Anthropic employees.\n\nI worry that METR is not independent enough because they have to carefully avoid ticking Anthropic off, lest their access be revoked.\n\nWe are not the same.", "name": "Nate Soares ⏹️", "handle": "So8res", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1935185891863273472/2RB6s6TS_200x200.jpg", "likes": 405, "rts": 21, "replies": 19, "views": 9599, "ts": 1792513615, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFlaPJboAA8iu_.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112574629164290233", "url": "https://x.com/XBOX/status/2112574629164290233", "text": "25 years of nostalgia in your hands. \n\nGet the XBOX Wireless Controller X25 Special Edition today: https://xbx.lv/4dKngOq", "name": "XBOX", "handle": "XBOX", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2111137016138407936/kRO4UxLa_200x200.jpg", "likes": 6075, "rts": 494, "replies": 171, "views": 612800, "ts": 1792512015, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112574569034694656/vid/avc1/1280x720/puZ2IZYlnrjNqGBB.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112574569034694656/vid/avc1/1920x1080/ozadgd2Q-kdCH3rF.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFfbYtWwAADgU4.jpg", "dur": 15}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.09, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112567049784271236", "url": "https://x.com/SirGlavan_/status/2112567049784271236", "text": "I'm especially interested in the agentic benchmarks. Strong BrowseComp and MCP-Atlas results suggest Ornith-1.5 could be worth testing on workflows involving research, tool selection, and multi-step execution.", "name": "JAYDEN™", "handle": "SirGlavan_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2089845866219589632/aEdG2e1-_200x200.jpg", "likes": 15, "rts": 11, "replies": 1, "views": 5467, "ts": 1792510208, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112553477457268799", "url": "https://x.com/ornith_/status/2112553477457268799", "text": "Aloha!🌺 Meet Ornith-1.5-122B: No Tradeoff Between Strong and Fast  \n\nStronger. Faster. Leaner. Ornith-1.5-122B delivers frontier-level capabilities with exceptional inference efficiency. With superior instruction following, stronger task decomposition, and deeper understanding of real-world workflows, it achieves state-of-the-art performance among open-source models of comparable size, while running on a single NVIDIA DGX card!!\n\nOpen weights under the MIT license.\nCoding \n✅SWE-bench Verified: 0.845 \n✅TB2.1: 0.813 \n✅CyberGym: 0.800 \n✅NL2Repo: 0.512 \nAgentic \n✅HLE: 0.446 \n✅BrowseComp: 0.785 \n✅MCP-Atlas: 0.746 \n✅Toolathlon: 0.708  \n\n🤗Hugging Face: https://huggingface.co/ornith-ai/Ornith-1.5-122B \nWe can’t wait to see what you build with Ornith-1.5-122B.", "name": "Ornith", "handle": "ornith_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2067467120544456704/qYuod4O1_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2375, "rts": 433, "replies": 177, "views": 1086684, "ts": 1792506973, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFMLvWbAAE3955.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.09, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112631097800499218", "url": "https://x.com/0xLagosaur/status/2112631097800499218", "text": "your agent read the whole file to find one function\n\nthe read costs thousands of tokens,\n\nthe search that would have found the same line costs hundreds\n\nan edit sits between them, because the old text and the new text both travel\n\nand the biggest thing in your window is usually test output nobody looked at,\n\nsetup noise and passing cases, a thousand tokens of nothing\n\nput those four numbers next to each other\n\nand the order of what to fix stops being a matter of taste\n\nsearching before reading, and silencing output nobody reads,\n\nbeat every clever thing you were going to do to your prompts", "name": "Lagosaur", "handle": "0xLagosaur", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2055749136947757056/wZRBHfGn_200x200.jpg", "likes": 34, "rts": 1, "replies": 2, "views": 1111, "ts": 1792525479, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112631017534078976/vid/avc1/480x852/3PHNWjXBd_4FHx66.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112631017534078976/vid/avc1/720x1280/JZOGl48dvgPxQdZa.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112631017534078976/img/qQEUYul32Bl6-fB7.jpg", "dur": 129}], "quote": {"id": "2112181706111295724", "url": "https://x.com/0xLagosaur/status/2112181706111295724", "text": "https://x.com/i/article/2112168217183428608", "name": "Lagosaur", "handle": "0xLagosaur", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2055749136947757056/wZRBHfGn_200x200.jpg", "likes": 20, "rts": 0, "replies": 0, "views": 6826, "ts": 1792418335, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.09, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112598233948320143", "url": "https://x.com/Rames_Jusso/status/2112598233948320143", "text": "Everyone sees a video and wishes they could recreate a caption style, pacing, etc\n\nNow you can using @HyperFrames_ studio\n\nMake great videos and apply your style and brand to give it your own twist.\n\nIt can automatically edit your existing content into new formats as well", "name": "James Russo", "handle": "Rames_Jusso", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1975631772495843329/iXCrGkfN_200x200.jpg", "likes": 21, "rts": 6, "replies": 3, "views": 1251, "ts": 1792517643, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112591698476077345", "url": "https://x.com/HyperFrames_/status/2112591698476077345", "text": "the editing techniques and styles you thought were unattainable\n\nnow just one reference prompt away:\n\n- the hook from an Instagram reel\n- the b-roll style from a TikTok\n- the captions from a YouTube Short\n\nthen automatically apply them to your footage with your story\n\nget started ↓", "name": "HyperFrames", "handle": "HyperFrames_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2050290878221291520/ZNexbFre_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1088, "rts": 327, "replies": 409, "views": 531306, "ts": 1792516085, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112590171086761984/vid/avc1/1280x720/9a9HgutVE8XZ3Wct.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112590171086761984/vid/avc1/1920x1080/e5kSl8cwWTskpJ66.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112590171086761984/img/BnUfiE2s8_ERaD6D.jpg", "dur": 52}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.09, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112580262697582750", "url": "https://x.com/zostaff/status/2112580262697582750", "text": "HOLY F*CKING SHIT SOME GUY BUILT A HOUND THAT TRACKS PUMP RINGS ON SOLANA AND NOBODY IS TALKING ABOUT IT\n\nrepo: http://github.com/localminimaa/tracehound\n\neveryone checks the coin. he checks the wallets that pump it\n\nhow it works inside\n\n> finds wallets that keep buying the same launches together and clusters them into rings\n> maps who funded each ring. one ring we caught: 20 wallets, 16 different funders. the money is spread on purpose so bubble maps don't link them\n> learns the ring's playbook: fresh dev wallet gets exactly 0.75 SOL, launches on meteora minutes later, ring wallets buy in the first slots\n> different funders every time. same 0.75 SOL. same hand\n\nthe playbook is the real juice. a ring can change wallets, funders, tickers. it can't change how it launches\n\n> a live watch follows ring wallets and alerts when a launch matches a known playbook\n> every token check names the ring wallets sitting in the early buyers\n\nand then the part nobody else does\n\n> every verdict is checked against the real price 24h later\n> 9 of 10 tokens it flagged were down within 24h\n> 5 of them lost 90%+\n> the ring's ALLOX: $16.3M at check -> $190K a day later\n> the one flagged token that went up stays in the table. misses are shown on purpose\n\nit also traces hacks across 9 chains and follows stolen money through bridges, but that's a whole separate thread\n\neverything is open source. read it, fork it, verify it\n\nwho's actually checking who's behind the coin before aping?", "name": "zostaff", "handle": "zostaff", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1995248671483482112/dZ1-JoSj_200x200.jpg", "likes": 31, "rts": 3, "replies": 4, "views": 1557, "ts": 1792513359, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112579914561888256/vid/avc1/1336x720/6Xd6dfrx5ST_UnCc.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112579914561888256/vid/avc1/2880x1550/gfPvc5wvAz2Nn5kD.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112579914561888256/img/94QcQZG_wVBnjA8B.jpg", "dur": 27}], "quote": {"id": "2112576400846737909", "url": "https://x.com/tracehoundpro/status/2112576400846737909", "text": "https://x.com/i/article/2112566452855160832", "name": "TraceHound", "handle": "tracehoundpro", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2110797500487458816/iYbF3WRK_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2, "rts": 0, "replies": 0, "views": 2780, "ts": 1792512438, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.09, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112598687796871204", "url": "https://x.com/angeloldesigns/status/2112598687796871204", "text": "✨ A designer’s dream: three AI agents designing in parallel on one canvas, while I sit back and watch the magic happen in Kaptea:\n• Agents work side by side and never step on each other\n• One activity sidebar: who’s doing what, what’s done, what needs you\n• Review every change: before and after, then Keep or Undo\n\nIf you design with agents, what’s the one thing your workflow can’t live without?", "name": "Angelo Libero", "handle": "angeloldesigns", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1543367697546756096/hF8-vm7w_200x200.jpg", "likes": 36, "rts": 1, "replies": 3, "views": 2083, "ts": 1792517752, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112598166784602112/vid/avc1/960x720/kAAUrJwkvk87EtxR.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112598166784602112/vid/avc1/2884x2160/5tFdPxSYGJp1TqSV.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112598166784602112/img/5vinvsVTsDW39qnu.jpg", "dur": 84}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.09, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112580153176203290", "url": "https://x.com/mariagpts/status/2112580153176203290", "text": "finally a robotics company that cares how the thing looks\n\nvoxel is genuinely beautiful, and the team brought in people from pixar to give him a personality\n\nif robots are going to live in our homes, i want mine to look like this", "name": "maria", "handle": "mariagpts", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2107879585178103808/JyLvfq8O_200x200.jpg", "likes": 30, "rts": 6, "replies": 0, "views": 412, "ts": 1792513333, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112565146354860151", "url": "https://x.com/make_robot_go/status/2112565146354860151", "text": "Introducing Voxel, a droid butler made by Tuesday Labs.", "name": "Ros Shinkle", "handle": "make_robot_go", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1761551110303825920/JvPQiGQd_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2181, "rts": 228, "replies": 203, "views": 1847987, "ts": 1792509755, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/960x720/cMYjra9bu_jYUTYR.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/2880x2160/glhkyiQ6K97Rmq93.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112564839251931136/img/GKLfsqVaQmO0B-kn.jpg", "dur": 89}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.09, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112627468687532455", "url": "https://x.com/ivanburazin/status/2112627468687532455", "text": "I'll be on @MTSlive shortly to discuss our Series B and how @daytonaio is building the agent cloud", "name": "Ivan Burazin", "handle": "ivanburazin", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1549052013178134529/FljtGcgj_200x200.jpg", "likes": 37, "rts": 1, "replies": 0, "views": 3835, "ts": 1792524613, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112578282084499682", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112578282084499682", "text": "DEEPSEEK INFERENCE | CHINA LABS BUY NVIDIA CHIPS | ANTHROPIC X CITRINI https://x.com/i/broadcasts/1yJAPwWLYwbGb", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 50, "rts": 9, "replies": 4, "views": 20939, "ts": 1792512886, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.08, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112635083911782568", "url": "https://x.com/Meemlah/status/2112635083911782568", "text": "spotted a winning trend → transformed it for my brand → rendered the final output.\n\nall before my morning coffee got cold thanks to @avastudio_ .", "name": "𝗦𝗔𝗕𝗜", "handle": "Meemlah", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1969594268059660288/qPUeM2_n_200x200.jpg", "likes": 22, "rts": 1, "replies": 7, "views": 321, "ts": 1792526429, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112635041192845312/vid/avc1/480x486/sqWqAmrpT7rQ1Xa2.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112635041192845312/vid/avc1/720x730/ujnUIo9T_sbISb_9.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112635041192845312/img/azQp52rkUZ72hwrf.jpg", "dur": 5}], "quote": {"id": "2112606581229769030", "url": "https://x.com/avastudio_/status/2112606581229769030", "text": "We just turned TikToks and Reels into a Claude Code task.\n\nMeet Ava Studio, for founders whose product is live but nobody knows it exists.\n\nGive your agent your product URL and let it research trends across 400,000+ TikToks, write scripts and create videos ready to post.", "name": "Ava Studio", "handle": "avastudio_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2060828052645384197/o5Z3NzuU_200x200.jpg", "likes": 381, "rts": 75, "replies": 88, "views": 202673, "ts": 1792519633, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112606467731943424/vid/avc1/1280x720/wBPNy4C8XvnT1Mr4.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112606467731943424/vid/avc1/1920x1080/0kVGCjlWFJaXfCpq.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112606467731943424/img/UhUfy5CUaqFygliU.jpg", "dur": 39}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.08, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112693968500847101", "url": "https://x.com/RealCandaceO/status/2112693968500847101", "text": "Here is a thread featuring the videos from today’s episode of who we believe is the same individual returning to the scene of Losee Rooftop 20 minutes later. As I explained on the show today, I think it is plausible that he dropped the screwdriver during this time.", "name": "Candace Owens", "handle": "RealCandaceO", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2008001395589316609/0QORb4sg_200x200.jpg", "likes": 3485, "rts": 470, "replies": 190, "views": 159464, "ts": 1792540468, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112693952956469248/vid/avc1/1280x720/MygpbB6rIQSzwkTL.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112693952956469248/vid/avc1/1920x1080/1iGH7z0DUbX_B9jX.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112693952956469248/img/oi2m9UY98pHiK9yG.jpg", "dur": 3}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.08, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112596663630250338", "url": "https://x.com/OPteemyst/status/2112596663630250338", "text": "Slowly, then all at once", "name": "Oukham", "handle": "OPteemyst", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1486545377633484801/BziWpI4j_200x200.jpg", "likes": 5120, "rts": 616, "replies": 155, "views": 2857089, "ts": 1792517269, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112596606843248640/vid/avc1/480x610/0kmW5K0boA8yx_Ar.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112596606843248640/vid/avc1/720x916/SuJLw3BFXE57_lpX.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112596606843248640/img/h7gatmLJ4-4_Dd52.jpg", "dur": 60}], "quote": {"id": "2112551927649018058", "url": "https://x.com/SawyerMerritt/status/2112551927649018058", "text": "Elon Musk in new interview with Walter Isaacson on the wealth he's created:\n\n\"A fundamental misunderstanding of economics arises because of conflating resource allocation and consumption; I've created. My so-called wealth is simply a percentage ownership in SpaceX and Tesla. And this is going to be taxed quite heavily, and there's not some magical way to avoid taxes. If there were I would know about it. At the end of the day, this will get whittled down, and a few generations from now, if money still matters, which I don't think it will, my descendants would have a tiny fraction of what I have.\"", "name": "Sawyer Merritt", "handle": "SawyerMerritt", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1837744842715082752/xH9vYixL_200x200.jpg", "likes": 3053, "rts": 359, "replies": 204, "views": 3128972, "ts": 1792506603, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112550486775574528/vid/avc1/720x740/IVY-zfHHYhRmL9g6.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112550486775574528/vid/avc1/1048x1080/ZUgkMG4w60plxaPE.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112550486775574528/img/vJQOpt-2OGMjqNBW.jpg", "dur": 97}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.08, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112593032952570094", "url": "https://x.com/cagyjan1/status/2112593032952570094", "text": "This is why they don't want to see me succeed. We are changing the game for the better!\n\nHere is the thing, our brand already works irl so they try to dismiss us as nothing, just a little thing, a tiny little brand. \n\nIt's not a little thing, that's why brands with more funding haven't done claw machines, stores, collaborations irl, toys, games and much more like we have.\n\nIt's not an idea, it's already in motion and while we haven't unlocked a massive amount of revenue YET, we are getting closer everyday and NFT holders will benefit.", "name": "cagy | youtube/cagyjan", "handle": "cagyjan1", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1943875331481296900/ZIL_YTCC_200x200.jpg", "likes": 25, "rts": 6, "replies": 1, "views": 1820, "ts": 1792516403, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112592485159735296/vid/avc1/720x1280/sxMO3rQmRDKjaurS.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112592485159735296/vid/avc1/2160x3840/cpnglE9Cj13wCsZu.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112592485159735296/img/x23HT33TEc9tyViN.jpg", "dur": 36}], "quote": {"id": "2112590410849878460", "url": "https://x.com/cagyjan1/status/2112590410849878460", "text": "Revenue Sharing NFTs!\n\nEarn a @sillykittiesco NFT for 2 weeks only! Top 5 players get a FREE mint!\n\nNFT holders earn a % of revenue from merch, stores, toys, claw machines, games & marketplace fees.\n\nPlay our first game\nhttp://playcafe.sillykitties.co\n\nWe're doing what no brand has done before! https://x.com/cagyjan1/status/2110586822766260464/video/1", "name": "cagy | youtube/cagyjan", "handle": "cagyjan1", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1943875331481296900/ZIL_YTCC_200x200.jpg", "likes": 31, "rts": 9, "replies": 4, "views": 3038, "ts": 1792515778, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2110586757582565376/vid/avc1/1558x720/jbRdvNnpvdwuEIHj.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2110586757582565376/vid/avc1/2772x1280/h0nHUyfdCMAIC-Zu.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2110586757582565376/img/2QBckxeMp_3nJp5M.jpg", "dur": 57}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.08, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112477947684585744", "url": "https://x.com/premierleague/status/2112477947684585744", "text": "Slick 🪄\n\n@LUFC", "name": "Premier League", "handle": "premierleague", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1742837199005954048/YGI6Kw7P_200x200.jpg", "likes": 8501, "rts": 569, "replies": 93, "views": 476057, "ts": 1792488965, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112477906840526848/vid/avc1/720x1280/XsQRT7sKReuYdbpF.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112477906840526848/vid/avc1/1080x1920/TJuHISdzEPzXQilK.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVEHfj3WwAAKlKn.jpg", "dur": 6}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.08, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112589618889756768", "url": "https://x.com/alex_prompter/status/2112589618889756768", "text": "\"Just buy more GPUs\" is the laziest idea in AI right now.\n\nYour agent isn't slow because it needs more compute. It's slow because it's starving for memory, and the HBM those GPUs need is sold out.\n\n@general_compute just stopped playing that game:\n→ GPUs read the prompt\n→ @positron_ai's memory-first chips write the answer\n→ One endpoint, one contract\n\nAtlas today, Titan next, live Q1 2027.\n\nMost infra teams will figure this out in two years. These guys already did.", "name": "Alex Prompter", "handle": "alex_prompter", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2066532957049769985/zzC81Zmq_200x200.jpg", "likes": 13, "rts": 7, "replies": 5, "views": 5419, "ts": 1792515589, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112585266854604957", "url": "https://x.com/general_compute/status/2112585266854604957", "text": "Our heterogeneous cloud just got better. We're announcing a cluster scale deployment of @positron_ai as our next partner.\n\nWe believe demand for fast inference will outstrip supply for the next decade. Our bet on Positron is another step towards getting fast inference for opensource models into builders' hands.\n\nHardware goes live Q1 2027.\n\nThanks to @mitesh711, @trsohmers and the whole Positron team! We're excited for this partnership.\n\nLFG!", "name": "General Compute", "handle": "general_compute", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2063265967774584832/y1U0qHB3_200x200.jpg", "likes": 830, "rts": 58, "replies": 108, "views": 234978, "ts": 1792514552, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112585087921377280/pu/vid/avc1/640x360/KX7QPT-I86P0SW2r.mp4?tag=12", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112585087921377280/pu/vid/avc1/1280x720/XBFGYfCEY_EsyfiI.mp4?tag=12", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/2112585087921377280/pu/img/EYiImymSTr1OyRJQ.jpg", "dur": 47}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112637579346800801", "url": "https://x.com/HarshithLucky3/status/2112637579346800801", "text": "something feels off with Opus 5.5 \n\nI want to run this cheetah pixel art test\n\nthis doesn’t prove anything about the nerf thing but I still want to re-run it and see if it generates this level of motion again...\n\nanyone else noticing the change?", "name": "Harshith", "handle": "HarshithLucky3", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1940482570484858880/dYD7sVKE_200x200.jpg", "likes": 26, "rts": 2, "replies": 3, "views": 2730, "ts": 1792527024, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2103120423005425972", "url": "https://x.com/HarshithLucky3/status/2103120423005425972", "text": "Claude Opus 5.5 High vs GPT 6 Astra Max\n\n> 640×360 pixel art of cheetah running\n\nlook at the difference", "name": "Harshith", "handle": "HarshithLucky3", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1940482570484858880/dYD7sVKE_200x200.jpg", "likes": 939, "rts": 35, "replies": 73, "views": 142439, "ts": 1790257957, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2103120094536818688/vid/avc1/720x806/qAaEBh5lWHD_QmrE.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2103120094536818688/vid/avc1/2160x2422/Qfm6e0jzkAsyRego.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2103120094536818688/img/fLP6SLOjsCo5OQyA.jpg", "dur": 12}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112619415841968255", "url": "https://x.com/SkiJr1/status/2112619415841968255", "text": "China Factory Direct | Mass ready-stock research assay kits, ship instantly!\nOur newest batch of high-purity research kits features custom coloured caps & standard labels. Ongoing factory production maintains sufficient inventory for fast global delivery.\n\n▫️ 99%+ Certified Purity Premium consistent quality to strengthen your brand ▫️ Stable Continuous Production Plenty stock on hand, immediate dispatch worldwide ▫️ OEM & Private Label Available Custom caps, labels, packaging and full kit branding\nSearching for a trusted manufacturer to expand your business? DM or visit our X profile to grab the 2026 wholesale catalog!\n\nFor research use only. Not for human consumption.", "name": "Lisa", "handle": "SkiJr1", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2099558821945655296/CvfeH50j_200x200.jpg", "likes": 18, "rts": 0, "replies": 11, "views": 449, "ts": 1792522693, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112619253035859968/vid/avc1/480x852/q_1OAOO9ydAuRrsv.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112619253035859968/vid/avc1/720x1280/E8Bqw5BMeAASSvBe.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112619253035859968/img/nUxrqK3mcRunmRxo.jpg", "dur": 22}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Research & Safety", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112623492579328219", "url": "https://x.com/itsarcvale/status/2112623492579328219", "text": "A 23-YEAR-OLD CLAIMS 240 CLAUDE CODE AGENTS DID A $175K ANALYST'S JOB IN ONE AFTERNOON. THE F*CKING TRICK IS ONE LOOP\n\nhis post this week:\n> 10 scouts, 9 extractors, 8 cross-checkers, 6 reconcilers, 3 judges\n> 120 company filings\n> every claim held against the exact source page\n> anything that doesn't match goes back as \"rewrite\"\n\ncan't verify the kid. the loop is real and you can build it tonight\n\nthe rule underneath ↓ an agent never grades its own work\n\nnow point it at earnings season\n\nyour bot reads a press release, grabs \"revenue up 12%\" and trades it. one wrong number and you just bought a headline that never existed\n\nthe split:\n→ the big model writes every claim with a page number\n→ a cheap model opens that exact page and checks it\n→ mismatch = rewrite, never a trade\n→ only claims that survive both reach your signals\n\nyou only step in three times:\n→ when a claim bounces twice\n→ when the filing and the press release disagree\n→ before anything goes near real money\n\nthe big model writes. the cheap one checks. nothing trades unverified\n\npaste this into Claude Code ↓\n\n\"Build earnings_check.py:\n1. Pull the latest 10-Q and earnings press release for [ticker] from SEC EDGAR.\n2. Have Opus extract every number (revenue, EPS, margins, guidance) with the exact page it came from.\n3. Have Haiku open that page and confirm each number. Mismatch → send back as rewrite.\n4. Loop until every claim matches, max 3 passes. Log every bounce to verify.log.\n5. Write only verified claims to signals.csv. Paper only, no orders.\nShow me the code first. Don't run anything until I say go.\"\n\none of these every night. tomorrow's builds on this one", "name": "Arcvale", "handle": "itsarcvale", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2104153950932934656/7lVoY59G_200x200.jpg", "likes": 14, "rts": 4, "replies": 7, "views": 425, "ts": 1792523665, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112623356721721344/vid/avc1/720x900/AxknNSMMpIZkeiOJ.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112623356721721344/vid/avc1/1080x1350/65d-0D_ipxzUMRCY.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112623356721721344/img/yCnH8tE83l8RmLgD.jpg", "dur": 18}], "quote": {"id": "2111774069783720195", "url": "https://x.com/Gyome1_/status/2111774069783720195", "text": "REA hit #1 on GitHub trending, and most people still run it inside a single chat\n\nSplit it into 4 subagents and one command takes a program you own from sealed binary to a tested rebuild with a match rate\n\nSet it up once, aim it at the next one: https://x.com/i/article/2111752926104375296", "name": "Gyomei", "handle": "Gyome1_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1962101558973177856/oOpe-HZg_200x200.jpg", "likes": 147, "rts": 19, "replies": 9, "views": 98554, "ts": 1792321147, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112688564605423705", "url": "https://x.com/HarryStebbings/status/2112688564605423705", "text": "Why the rise of open models does not denigrate the market for closed models\n\n“When you are in a market that big, predicting with any precision the mix between closed tokens and open tokens is irrelevant.\n\nAll those different use cases, from consumers up through enterprise and government, are going to want intelligence of different types and different flavours.\n\nWe are investors in both Anthropic and Fireworks, the closed tokens and the open tokens. I think both are going to be huge.” @spdholakia\n\nLove to hear your thoughts @ClementDelangue @lqiao @dylan522p @ionstoica", "name": "Harry Stebbings", "handle": "HarryStebbings", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1862557919717265409/2xIkJF_g_200x200.jpg", "likes": 9, "rts": 1, "replies": 10, "views": 4578, "ts": 1792539180, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112217793328185344/vid/avc1/1280x720/kQ105Q-Wk3C1N5sx.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112217793328185344/vid/avc1/1920x1080/UGxr90IALVUYcDSp.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112217793328185344/img/wfugGQXypTrE18zf.jpg", "dur": 34}], "quote": {"id": "2112184320735510556", "url": "https://x.com/HarryStebbings/status/2112184320735510556", "text": "Pricing in venture is wilder than ever.\n\n$100M pre-seed is now normal.\n\nBessemer just raised $1.75BN for “early” and $4BN for growth.\n\nSo can you even do seed today without $1BN?\n\n- Is capital truly one of the last remaining moats?\n- Do all small seed funds and mid-sized firms just fade into irrelevance?\n- Does entry price matter anymore when there are $TRN companies…\n- Is this real or a bubble that is about to burst\n\nI sat down with @spdholakia to discuss this and have added my notes from the discussion below.\n\n1. This Is a Supercycle Like Never Before\n\nSameer has spent 31 years in software and has felt magic only a handful of times. A trillion-dollar supercycle followed every one of those moments, and he notes that it does not happen very often.\n\nWhat is different and what is similar to prior cycles @altcap @infoarbitrage\n\n2. Capital Is a Moat Today\n\nMarkets pick winners and the choice becomes a self-fulfilling prophecy, as it did when developers settled on SendGrid and Twilio. In legal AI, big law firms name just two major providers. Capital lets leaders scale at an extraordinary pace and build a brand, which draws talent and customers in a reinforcing flywheel.\n\nDo you agree with this @venkyganesan @dafrankel\n\n3. Who Wins and Who Loses in the Future of Venture Capital?\n\nAs industries professionalize, firms must be either a giant global platform that consolidates or an extreme specialist, such as an early-stage AI investor in San Francisco. Sameer counts Bessemer as a big global platform. Firms caught in between face a hard world to make money.\n\nIs it go big or go home @rodriscoll @rabois @chetanp\n\n4. The Rationale for Why Anthropic Would Compete With the Hyperscalers and Why We Invested\n\nAs in the cloud era, AI would be massively capital intensive, so it would consolidate to a handful of players with hundreds of apps on top. Microsoft had partnered with OpenAI and Google was building Gemini, while AWS had an undistinctive internal model and had just invested heavily in Anthropic.\n\n5. Why Price Does Not Matter in a World of AI and the Metric That Truly Determines Value\n\nBessemer invested in Abridge at $5M of ARR for a $700M to $800M valuation, in Anthropic at roughly 150 times current ARR, and led Legora's $1.8B round at $20M of ARR. Sameer judges these deals on what the company can become in the next twelve months.\n\nHow has your relationship to price changed in a world of AI @mignano @mmurph\n\n6. Why the Rise of Open Models Does Not Denigrate the Market for Closed Models\n\nIn a market this large, predicting the mix between closed and open tokens with any precision is irrelevant. Consumers, enterprises and governments will all want different flavors of intelligence. Bessemer has invested in both Anthropic and Fireworks to hold exposure to closed and open tokens.\n\nLove to hear how you think about this @lqiao @bernhardsson\n\n7. Why It Is a Permanent Structural Shift That Companies Will Stay Private for Longer, but Why It Will Open in 2028\n\nWith more dollars and more firms in private venture, companies will stay private longer, and most of the run-up in this boom will happen in private markets. Sameer still expects an unlock in IPOs later next year and in 2028.\n\nLove to hear your thoughts on this @bgurley and how you see it evolving in 24 months?\n\n(links in comments)", "name": "Harry Stebbings", "handle": "HarryStebbings", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1862557919717265409/2xIkJF_g_200x200.jpg", "likes": 142, "rts": 13, "replies": 43, "views": 126008, "ts": 1792418959, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112490376334561605", "url": "https://x.com/DuaFatimaAi/status/2112490376334561605", "text": "Open Gemini, Grok or GPT Image 2.0\n② Upload your image\n③ Paste the prompt\n④ Generate your image and video\n\nPrompt given below ⤵️", "name": "Dua Fatima", "handle": "DuaFatimaAi", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2085266884497448960/5b2fwBj7_200x200.jpg", "likes": 23, "rts": 0, "replies": 19, "views": 666, "ts": 1792491928, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112490130707742720/vid/avc1/480x270/tqH8tOK8Ju93hkqG.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112490130707742720/vid/avc1/480x270/tqH8tOK8Ju93hkqG.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112490130707742720/img/wHQBdw_ElSg0ac9Z.jpg", "dur": 25}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112577924566319259", "url": "https://x.com/startupideaspod/status/2112577924566319259", "text": "Personal agent arbitrage starts at $1,000 a month. Level 4 is a startup.\n\nLevel 1: Mining. Find the gold in other people's groups, on Marketplace, and on IG.\n\nLevel 2: Own the list. Take it off the platform. Clean it. Price it. Make it a trusted list.\n\nLevel 3: Own the room. Own the Facebook group, the niche IG account, and the storefronts.\n\nLevel 4: Build technology. Make the SaaS or vertical agent that automates the workflow end to end.\n\nLevel 4 needs 3 things first: an audience, clean data, and a workflow that you understand.\n\nStart at level 1 now. For the audience, use Muse to research accounts and formats and get content ideas.", "name": "The Startup Ideas Podcast (SIP) 🧃", "handle": "startupideaspod", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1955709395553124352/b_NlfUL__200x200.jpg", "likes": 31, "rts": 3, "replies": 3, "views": 3559, "ts": 1792512801, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112577745951854592/vid/avc1/1280x720/viQDEDG8IV7dzN0G.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112577745951854592/vid/avc1/1920x1080/U6qPlGA_giqszVzH.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112577745951854592/img/-kupENf1OfqUmpKs.jpg", "dur": 195}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112594926655422581", "url": "https://x.com/spectnfa/status/2112594926655422581", "text": "HOLY SH*T, ELON MUSK'S TEAM SHARED 120+ WAYS TO USE GROK BOT, AND GOOGLE'S EX-CEO SAYS THIS IS THE YEAR TO LEARN AGENTS\n\nmaking money with agents gets easier once you see how real teams run them\n\nthe people who build grok bot wrote it all down. here's where everything lives ↓\n\n17 GUIDES\nsales, support, recruiting, engineering, legal, design, product\n\nhttps://x.ai/bot/guides\n\n56 USE CASES\nready-made jobs you can hand to a bot: 13 marketing, 10 sales, 6 general, 5 ops & finance, 5 product, 5 engineering, 4 support, 4 recruiting, 4 life\n\nbrowse + add in one click: https://x.ai/bot/use-cases\nsame roles with starter prompts to copy: https://docs.x.ai/grok-bot/use-cases\n\nMARKETPLACE\n\nbots built by the grok bot team: https://x.ai/bot/marketplace/from-grok-bot-team\n\nby category\n\nsales: https://x.ai/bot/marketplace/sales\nmarketing: https://x.ai/bot/marketplace/marketing\nengineering: https://x.ai/bot/marketplace/engineering\nproduct: https://x.ai/bot/marketplace/product\noperations: https://x.ai/bot/marketplace/operations\ndesign: https://x.ai/bot/marketplace/design\nrecruiting: https://x.ai/bot/marketplace/recruiting-people\npersonal: https://x.ai/bot/marketplace/personal\n\nDOCS\n\nget started: https://docs.x.ai/grok-bot/get-started\ntag bot on X: https://docs.x.ai/grok-bot/tag-on-x\nskills + routines: https://docs.x.ai/grok-bot/skills-routines-and-automations\nteam bots: https://docs.x.ai/grok-bot/team-bots\nsecurity + approvals: https://docs.x.ai/grok-bot/approvals-security-and-privacy\n\nsave this! the guides are free to read\n\nthen study the article below on setting up grok bot with the spacexai engineers workflow ↓", "name": "spect", "handle": "spectnfa", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2088997909928812544/iegJFfNm_200x200.jpg", "likes": 33, "rts": 1, "replies": 4, "views": 707, "ts": 1792516855, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112593492668989441/vid/avc1/1280x720/eMZ43AO7g257rmu7.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112593492668989441/vid/avc1/1922x1080/bYymfZS5KWKtX8dA.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112593492668989441/img/zJWTI1ytgdV8EwnB.jpg", "dur": 26}], "quote": {"id": "2112574886421901822", "url": "https://x.com/unicodef1wn/status/2112574886421901822", "text": "I put together one guide for anyone who wants a workflow like the SpaceXSI team's.\n\nOne message builds your whole Grok Bot setup. Plus the team's rules, prompt habits, routines and permissions. Every setup is a block you paste.\n\n16-min read. Save it ↓ https://x.com/i/article/2112449845566877696", "name": "unicode", "handle": "unicodef1wn", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2069360360763576321/Id-DSoyU_200x200.jpg", "likes": 125, "rts": 3, "replies": 30, "views": 54763, "ts": 1792512077, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112609823976296645", "url": "https://x.com/mojunel/status/2112609823976296645", "text": "A 24-year-old launched a faceless YouTube channel 13 days ago. In the first month, he has already accumulated $4,000, but he has not shot a single frame.\n\nHis investment: a $20 subscription to Claude. No camera, no editor, no voice of his own.\n\nTHE SYSTEM WORKS LIKE THIS:\n\n- Claude writes the full script from one topic prompt\n- an AI voice narrates it\n- an AI tool generates the animation and the visuals\n- one template, repeated forever: “the economics of owning an airport” / “...a private jet” / “...a hospital”\n- it publishes on a schedule while he sleeps\n\nThe first 12 days, from zero:\n\n-> “Why a Fan Can Kill You” > 272,000 views\n-> “Economics of Owning a Sports Team” > 26,000 views in 7 days\n-> “Economics of Owning a Shopping Mall” > 70,000 views in 8 days\nsubscribers > 4,300\n-> month one pace > ~$4,000\n\nAnd it’s replicable. one template. one voice. one illustration style. infinite topics\n\nHe didn’t become a creator. He built a press that prints episodes.\n\nThe whole stack is public. Everyone has the same $20 Claude. He just pointed it at a niche and refused to stop publishing.", "name": "Mojunel.eth", "handle": "mojunel", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2101104367445401600/YqIoOt7o_200x200.jpg", "likes": 28, "rts": 1, "replies": 5, "views": 1230, "ts": 1792520407, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112608360809840640/vid/avc1/480x852/9YXxLoGGE_-C2XA0.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112608360809840640/vid/avc1/720x1280/8GeQWka58pGi1pQd.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112608360809840640/img/isLD_MHvLAxOjfmi.jpg", "dur": 46}], "quote": {"id": "2111100246189089085", "url": "https://x.com/mojunel/status/2111100246189089085", "text": "https://x.com/i/article/2111091990523752448", "name": "Mojunel.eth", "handle": "mojunel", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2101104367445401600/YqIoOt7o_200x200.jpg", "likes": 32, "rts": 0, "replies": 1, "views": 4698, "ts": 1792160495, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112614976787812802", "url": "https://x.com/MireloAI/status/2112614976787812802", "text": "SFX 2.0 is now live on @morphic 🫰", "name": "Mirelo", "handle": "MireloAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2056684878804987904/SKxWDUAT_200x200.jpg", "likes": 24, "rts": 4, "replies": 2, "views": 1210, "ts": 1792521635, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112560095699873835", "url": "https://x.com/morphic/status/2112560095699873835", "text": "Mirelo SFX 2.0 is now live on @morphic.\n\nAttach a video to build a new soundtrack that follows the action, or describe a sound to generate it from text.\n\nKeep the dialogue, guide the sounds you want, and work with audio or video up to 10 minutes long.\n\nhttps://morphic.com/", "name": "Morphic", "handle": "morphic", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1842802567295668224/5a_rsbBc_200x200.jpg", "likes": 34, "rts": 8, "replies": 7, "views": 2389, "ts": 1792508550, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112559394525437952/vid/avc1/1280x720/dIgipsewJ4r0QyO2.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112559394525437952/vid/avc1/1920x1080/q-wdooVpV8em16zF.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112559394525437952/img/8Q0uyxcYETt7SGIB.jpg", "dur": 31}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112610389393551579", "url": "https://x.com/r1VeN2k/status/2112610389393551579", "text": "42K PEOPLE THOUGHT THIS AI CHARACTER WAS A REAL GUY\n\none fedora, one mustache you can see from space, and an instagram at 367K followers on 43 posts.\n\n\"I'M ROSTAM. I DANCE, I ENTERTAIN AND I PLAY FREESTYLE FOOTBALL.\"\n\nthat's his website. a persian post called him an iranian guy who moved abroad. 42K views, and the replies are still arguing whether he exists.\n\nhe doesn't. his profile carries no \"AI-generated\" label, and the website never mentions ai.\n\nwhere the money sits:\n→ the website exists for one line: \"business inquiries & collaborations\"\n→ youtube, tiktok, instagram and x all point back to it\n→ his bio already tags a second character, sohrab. one face became a cast\n\ntwo things worth knowing before you copy it:\n→ \"is he real?\" is the engine. every argument in the comments is free reach\n→ instagram's rules require a label on realistic ai video. skipping it risks penalties, not just arguments\n\nall six ways ai characters actually earn are in my pinned article.\n\nwould you label your character as ai, or let people argue?", "name": "riVeN", "handle": "r1VeN2k", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1951018334310248448/GdXyG6vJ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 24, "rts": 3, "replies": 4, "views": 627, "ts": 1792520541, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112610324620681216/vid/avc1/480x852/VmpsGT1Ni8h66qLl.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112610324620681216/vid/avc1/720x1280/0tdHBJlP8UgHMvxy.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112610324620681216/img/owg_zn5I9ITEvSA9.jpg", "dur": 13}], "quote": {"id": "2111165596343615738", "url": "https://x.com/r1VeN2k/status/2111165596343615738", "text": "$43 in. About $235,000 out in 10 days, to the wallet listed as the coin's creator. None of it came from views.\n\n6 AI characters, 6 ways they actually earn.\n\nWhich would you build first: the character, or the thing it sells? https://x.com/i/article/2111161830932615168", "name": "riVeN", "handle": "r1VeN2k", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1951018334310248448/GdXyG6vJ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 19, "rts": 1, "replies": 5, "views": 5611, "ts": 1792176076, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112535261393342488", "url": "https://x.com/Nazik2053/status/2112535261393342488", "text": "THE MOST DANGEROUS AI ANALYST IS THE ONE THAT SOUNDS RIGHT.\n\nOne wrong margin. One missing minus sign. Last year's guidance slipped into this year's summary. The prose can be immaculate while the conclusion is garbage\n\nThis is the Claude Code research setup worth building: put a source check between the agent's draft and the report you actually read\n\nGive the work five separate roles:\n> scouts collect the original documents\n> extractors turn passages into individual claims\n> cross-checkers reopen the cited pages\n> reconcilers investigate disagreements\n> judges decide what can move forward and what needs a human\n\nEvery claim travels with its evidence: source file, exact page, supporting quote, reporting period and units. A link to a 200-page PDF doesn't count as showing your work\n\nThen make the rejection path explicit. Wrong period? Rewrite. Unsupported figure? Rewrite. Conflicting sources? Flag the conflict. Missing evidence? Keep it unresolved\n\nWrite the reason into verify.log and return it to the agent that produced the claim. Cap the retries. A stubborn disagreement goes to a person instead of looping until two models finally agree\n\nThe draft and the check should be separate jobs. Use code for arithmetic, dates and unit checks where possible. Use a reviewer for whether the cited passage actually supports the sentence\n\nHere's the starter instruction:\n\n\"Build a source-grounded company research workflow. Preserve originals in raw/. Give each claim a source file, page, quote, period and units. Separate drafting from verification. Log failures, allow two rewrite attempts, and escalate unresolved claims. Save the report and its claim ledger as Markdown for my Obsidian vault. Show the plan before running.\"\n\nThe 3D clip illustrates that workflow. It isn't a speed benchmark, and a verifier can still miss the same thing the writer missed. Agent teams also add token cost and coordination work, so start with one document and inspect the failures\n\nThe useful output is a report you can trace back to the page - including the parts the system couldn't settle.", "name": "Nazar", "handle": "Nazik2053", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2081786582852374528/U40IQu7b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 26, "rts": 0, "replies": 13, "views": 696, "ts": 1792502629, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112505837302284288/vid/avc1/720x900/Nn7cwFBs2N2d4HuD.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112505837302284288/vid/avc1/1080x1350/OkCvbPe3x3UM8tsm.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112505837302284288/img/tiC5-dcrjK2vzFMF.jpg", "dur": 30}], "quote": {"id": "2110757128050745432", "url": "https://x.com/Nazik2053/status/2110757128050745432", "text": "https://x.com/i/article/2110633972719812608", "name": "Nazar", "handle": "Nazik2053", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2081786582852374528/U40IQu7b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 8, "rts": 4, "replies": 1, "views": 7436, "ts": 1792078689, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112635229475344830", "url": "https://x.com/xtzhou/status/2112635229475344830", "text": "When we backed @RadicalNumerics, the bet was that one general model could learn the language of biology, the same way LLMs did for text. Today Omnii-1 beats AlphaGenome, designs antibodies and cancer vaccine candidates, and designed a phage covered by @carlzimmer in @NYTimes. All from one model. 🧬", "name": "Peter Zhou", "handle": "xtzhou", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1905114230824820736/x-DBN7N0_200x200.jpg", "likes": 28, "rts": 3, "replies": 0, "views": 1722, "ts": 1792526464, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112580926651904379", "url": "https://x.com/exnx/status/2112580926651904379", "text": "Introducing Omnii-1, our most powerful genome language model, and a major step toward general biological intelligence\n\nIn a world first, Omnii-1 designed the first AI-generated bacteriophages to be administered to a human patient with an antibiotic-resistant infection under compassionate use", "name": "Eric Nguyen", "handle": "exnx", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1640862340517335040/qcpMIN_b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 926, "rts": 163, "replies": 95, "views": 460874, "ts": 1792513517, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112578540013330432/vid/avc1/1280x720/o7F7SW5uTq0n6Cki.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112578540013330432/vid/avc1/1920x1080/PQ3lBUGHdIKOCD3U.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112578540013330432/img/iIkujuAjkAiQkxwh.jpg", "dur": 155}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112476697526149620", "url": "https://x.com/Turki_alalshikh/status/2112476697526149620", "text": "الفنان الكبير فضل شاكر وصل الرياض ❤️🙏🏼😎", "name": "TURKI ALALSHIKH", "handle": "Turki_alalshikh", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2063576818079199232/gLjJRw20_200x200.jpg", "likes": 6257, "rts": 576, "replies": 1087, "views": 2089858, "ts": 1792488667, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112476550448791552/vid/avc1/720x1280/p92A71nxbwivesMS.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112476550448791552/vid/avc1/1080x1920/2bdic32vio6AvhV3.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112476550448791552/img/6h69dKVbke02uwtu.jpg", "dur": 43}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112614258244743314", "url": "https://x.com/TechByMarkandey/status/2112614258244743314", "text": "AI agents could soon have their own Postgres databases without needing much memory.\n\nThat’s what makes PGX interesting.\n\n→ Just ~0.7 MB per idle database\n→ Up to 100× less idle memory\n→ 1,000 databases in only 659 MB RAM\n→ No separate containers needed for each database\n\nIt’s built in Rust, free, and open source.\n\nThis could make it much easier and cheaper to give every AI agent its own database.", "name": "Markandey Sharma", "handle": "TechByMarkandey", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2108632613602942976/O07ORNDX_200x200.jpg", "likes": 16, "rts": 0, "replies": 12, "views": 13985, "ts": 1792521464, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112579971952910540", "url": "https://x.com/alxshp/status/2112579971952910540", "text": "🚨Introducing a new database: PGX 🐘\n\nPostgres for AI agents. In Rust.  http://pgx.dev \n\nOne runtime. Thousands of Postgres databases.\n\n⚡ Up to 100× less idle memory\n⚡ 1,000 databases in just 659 MB RAM\n⚡ Clone a 674 MB database in 85 ms\n⚡ ~0.7 MB per idle database\n\nRUST. OPEN SOURCE. FREE.\n\nNo containers per database.\nNo heavyweight instances.\nNo production baggage.\n\nReal Postgres. Built to be disposable.\n\nhttps://x.com/alxshp/status/2110049413070831817", "name": "alex shapalov", "handle": "alxshp", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1978552796988493824/lEtPOGNq_200x200.jpg", "likes": 853, "rts": 71, "replies": 72, "views": 59236, "ts": 1792513289, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112372069308694529/vid/avc1/1190x720/6WoEAoIuaIto8rEy.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112372069308694529/vid/avc1/3572x2160/RJhhw9-cEEJh3GeA.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112372069308694529/img/n5MlTVsknCrF5wOq.jpg", "dur": 15}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112628944365302250", "url": "https://x.com/amirshanehsaz/status/2112628944365302250", "text": "I can't thank the team @adaptyvbio enough! Claude is a major accelerant and enabler of molecule design, but none of that matters until you see the results in the lab. These scorpion toxins are very tricky to work with and the Adaptyv team was able to quickly express some of them in-house which gave us a lot more confidence in our results 🦂", "name": "Amir Shanehsazzadeh", "handle": "amirshanehsaz", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1469848771303378946/HiHJVs70_200x200.jpg", "likes": 23, "rts": 5, "replies": 0, "views": 1194, "ts": 1792524965, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112621921216971185", "url": "https://x.com/adaptyvbio/status/2112621921216971185", "text": "We're excited to share results from our latest wet lab campaign with @AnthropicAI and @citrini.\n\nClaude designed novel proteins to neutralize scorpion toxins and we tested 211 of these protein designs in our automated wet lab. 17 of them showed binding to the toxins in our experiments, with all data now available on @proteinbase.\n\nThis is a great example of what we're building towards: A world where anyone can run drug discovery campaigns on our automated wet lab.", "name": "Adaptyv Bio", "handle": "adaptyvbio", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1968723857700761600/shLzBHal_200x200.jpg", "likes": 284, "rts": 46, "replies": 12, "views": 16900, "ts": 1792523291, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112621406861017088/vid/avc1/1280x720/Zp0tS8GdC3_T1Us6.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112621406861017088/vid/avc1/1920x1080/MBEvM6baCEzTnK17.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112621406861017088/img/usSY2nDSmCwL_nee.jpg", "dur": 5}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112546053488828521", "url": "https://x.com/evermind/status/2112546053488828521", "text": "Agent Memory: A Real-World Use Case on Rokid AI Glasses\n\nYour next conversation with your AI glasses shouldn’t start from zero.\n\nA community builder has brought EverOS Cloud to @RokidGlobal glasses, giving a wearable assistant a memory that carries across conversations.\n\nAs you use it, saved details and preferences can help it respond with more relevant context, without making you explain everything again.\n\nWe love seeing our community bring long-term memory into everyday life, on devices you can actually wear.\n\nBuild something of your own. Subscribe to EverOS Cloud Pro now and get 3× the standard monthly usage for your first 6 months.\n\nhttps://everos.evermind.ai", "name": "EverMind", "handle": "evermind", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2030792985101926401/ia9mNmWL_200x200.png", "likes": 34, "rts": 2, "replies": 5, "views": 19671, "ts": 1792505203, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112540983095386112/vid/avc1/1280x720/s2aonOHs9RSmnpCf.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112540983095386112/vid/avc1/3840x2160/cxakCtMnNpK6cnsp.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112540983095386112/img/DUOJPupngWAQwC8j.jpg", "dur": 65}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.06, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112552439505109184", "url": "https://x.com/desertantlabs/status/2112552439505109184", "text": "Your app can sort a camera roll into albums or collections without uploading a single photo.\n\nOur image classification model, Eye, tags each photo by type and scene, from screenshots and receipts to beaches and dogs, all on device.\n\nEye runs on Android, Linux, Windows, iPhone, Mac and in the browser, through our SDK for Swift, Kotlin and JavaScript:\nhttp://desertant.com/models/eye", "name": "Desert Ant Labs", "handle": "desertantlabs", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093763744052445184/opIqrYrc_200x200.jpg", "likes": 23, "rts": 1, "replies": 11, "views": 924, "ts": 1792506725, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112551922670415872/vid/avc1/720x720/85eC7GHhY9dYGlVB.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112551922670415872/vid/avc1/1440x1440/bpoeIV8zT043dg6J.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112551922670415872/img/GPObexALddl7IOnL.jpg", "dur": 12}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.05, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112719571232977019", "url": "https://x.com/onloglogn/status/2112719571232977019", "text": "We just added @deepseek_ai's V4.1-Flash-1017 to RSI-Inference Bench http://rsi-inference.com , and it's now the #1 open model  🐳\n\nIt surpasses GLM-5.3 to take #8 on the leaderboard.\n\n- Day-0 support: 7th, hidden tests passed 35% → 62% (Pass@1 still at 0%)\n- Inference optimization: 7th, 1.23× speed-up", "name": "Ruixiang Zhang", "handle": "onloglogn", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1859067710615023616/ydbVmgo1_200x200.jpg", "likes": 15, "rts": 3, "replies": 2, "views": 1421, "ts": 1792546572, "media": [{"type": "gif", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/tweet_video/HVHi0PSa0AArGnk.mp4", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/tweet_video/HVHi0PSa0AArGnk.mp4", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/tweet_video_thumb/HVHi0PSa0AArGnk.jpg", "dur": 0}], "quote": {"id": "2111375640717033777", "url": "https://x.com/deepseek_ai/status/2111375640717033777", "text": "🚀 DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 is here!\n\nStronger benchmark performance, faster task completion, and shorter outputs than the previous version—a Pareto improvement in performance and cost. Now live on our website, app, and API.\n\n🛠️ Optimized for @DeepSeekHarness, Tencent CodeBuddy, WorkBuddy, and more. Upgrade to DeepSeek Harness v0.2.1-rc.1 or later for the best experience with the new model.\n\n1/4", "name": "DeepSeek", "handle": "deepseek_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1717417613775757312/Uk1zNOj4_200x200.jpg", "likes": 36930, "rts": 4122, "replies": 1605, "views": 7710970, "ts": 1792226154, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HU0b65KbsAAypqr.jpg?name=orig"}, {"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HU0b7UfbwAAGXNH.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.05, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112579947298762946", "url": "https://x.com/nereasolenne/status/2112579947298762946", "text": "every home robot i've seen so far looks like something i'd lock in the garage before going to sleep\n\nvoxel is the first one i'd actually leave in the living room\n\nit puts your stuff back where it belongs, finds your sunglasses, waters your plants, and apparently fluffs the pillows way more than necessary\n\nonly 999 numbered series-1 units, $200 to reserve one", "name": "nerea", "handle": "nereasolenne", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2094330461057073153/EpsIlfKY_200x200.jpg", "likes": 32, "rts": 4, "replies": 0, "views": 680, "ts": 1792513283, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112565146354860151", "url": "https://x.com/make_robot_go/status/2112565146354860151", "text": "Introducing Voxel, a droid butler made by Tuesday Labs.", "name": "Ros Shinkle", "handle": "make_robot_go", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1761551110303825920/JvPQiGQd_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2181, "rts": 228, "replies": 203, "views": 1849470, "ts": 1792509755, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/960x720/cMYjra9bu_jYUTYR.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/2880x2160/glhkyiQ6K97Rmq93.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112564839251931136/img/GKLfsqVaQmO0B-kn.jpg", "dur": 89}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.05, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112575270498754648", "url": "https://x.com/RaghuRaghuram/status/2112575270498754648", "text": "We believe solving dexterous manipulation is one of the largest opportunities in robotics. Eka has built a Vision-Force-Action model that combines visual perception with force feedback from its robotic hands.\n\nVery excited to be partnering with @pulkitology, @haarnoja, and backing the @EkaRobotics team!", "name": "Raghu Raghuram", "handle": "RaghuRaghuram", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1399724601970671616/B4sklL4p_200x200.jpg", "likes": 37, "rts": 1, "replies": 2, "views": 3356, "ts": 1792512168, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112564529905221861", "url": "https://x.com/pulkitology/status/2112564529905221861", "text": "@EkaRobotics has raised a $150M Series A.\n\nGenerality v/s Performance is the fundamental tension at the frontier of robotics. Generality without performance is just a prototype. Performance without generality is just a single-purpose tool.\n\nCustomers shouldn’t have to choose. Eka breaks the tradeoff. Powered by our Vision-Force-Action (VFA) model, we deliver the performance and versatility customers need to put robots to work every day.\n\nEka is built on three convictions: \n⚡️Force is the language of manipulation. \n 🚀 Reinforcement learning is how dexterous manipulation scales. \n🎂 System 1—fast, reliable physical execution—is the bottleneck to solve.\n\nWith this funding, we will scale our model and accelerate customer deployments.\n\nGrateful to be building alongside a dream team and investors who share our ambition.", "name": "Pulkit Agrawal", "handle": "pulkitology", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/952619389857153025/Uhr_wfXH_200x200.jpg", "likes": 768, "rts": 81, "replies": 63, "views": 74233, "ts": 1792509608, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112558017560387585/vid/avc1/1280x720/DNbO508h66HSSQW0.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112558017560387585/vid/avc1/1920x1080/sFqUGJOXTFpyLjOs.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112558017560387585/img/dzODOZVG31Ix3Bko.jpg", "dur": 24}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.05, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}]);